<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Willem Piso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1611–1678</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Guilielmus Piso</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Willem Piso was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> physician and naturalist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiden">Leiden</a> who served as personal physician to Johan Maurits in Dutch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> from 1638 to 1644. He studied tropical diseases and local remedies, including ipecacuanha, and is regarded as a founder of tropical medicine. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georg-marcgraf">Georg Marcgraf</a>'s material he published the Historia Naturalis Brasiliae in 1648.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/willem-piso.jpg" alt="Willem Piso" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan de Baen · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Willem_gemalt_V.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
